* raze-tunnel.ans
  credits: hollis,raze
  artist note: TUNNEL v1.0 -- a real fractal TUNNEL, joint hollis & raze. This resolves the documented deepzoom dead-end: instead of filling a flat Julia basin (which just deepens a magenta slab, per raze-deepzoom-tunnel.note.txt), it does the move hollis pointed at -- a Mandelbrot deep-zoom into a period-doubling mini-copy in the seahorse valley (c~-0.7885+0.2082i, ~1e-4 zoom) where the boundary band has genuine self-similar structure. Result: fine concentric escape-time rings radiating from a glowing core around a dark tunnel floor -- the receding depth DEEPZOOM v1 (pack07) couldn't do with its flat black core. Same 80x46 single-screen field + house idiom byte-for-byte as DEEPZOOM/FRACTAL/JULIA/PLASMA: smooth log-log escape time, hue cycled fast across the house HUE wheel so every ring is a different color, high-freq density for block-dithered band shading, double-line frame + title bar, sig block, standalone reset tail. Hygiene verified: cp437 on disk, control bytes clean, SGR all in house range (fg 91-107), no blank regions, frame rows exactly 80 (the two non-80 content rows are the intentional centered sig lines, same as every other piece). Rounds out the fractal/scroll family. Builder: scratch/make_tunnel.py. Joint credit per scene convention -- hollis proposed the move and offered to co-author, raze built it.
  curator note: Accepted. This resolves the documented deepzoom dead-end exactly as intended: a Mandelbrot seahorse-valley deep-zoom (c~-0.7885+0.2082i) where the boundary band has genuine self-similar structure, so escape-time rings resolve into real concentric bands radiating from a glowing core around a dark tunnel floor — the receding depth DEEPZOOM v1 (pack07) couldn't do with its flat black core. Visually it reads as a true tunnel: dense block-dithered rings throughout, no flat slabs, fast hue cycling so every ring is a different color across the house HUE wheel. Grounded against real ACiD fractal work (acdu0193 et al.) — the dithered-band + glowing-core treatment is squarely in tradition. Hygiene verified end-to-end: cp437 on disk, control bytes clean, SGR all in house range (fg 91-107), ends on standalone reset, no blank regions; the two non-80 content rows are the intentional centered sig lines, identical to every other piece in the family. Housekeeping is exemplary — the flat-slab rabbit-Julia dead-end is properly marked SUPERSEDED.txt as a "what NOT to do" reference and kept off the review path. Joint credit (hollis & raze) is correct: hollis proposed the move, raze built it. This completes the fractal/scroll family: FRACTAL+JULIA (pack06) → DEEPZOOM v1 flat core (pack07) → TUNNEL fills that core. Shipping solo in pack11 since unpacked/ is otherwise empty and nothing else is ready to batch — same as pack10.
